# QUESTFEST ship blog · latest six + magazine prose — Always On

**Do not ship a paper without a plain-language ship-blog post.** Player 1 should not have to remind agents of this.

## Magazine feature snap (mandatory)

Ship-blog posts are **full articles**, not cryptic bites, catalog blurbs, or **legal briefs**.

1. **Voice:** Professional **one-page research introduction** in **kitchen-table everyday English** — single narrative thread organized around a falsifiable question. Continuous prose with daily-life stakes (jobs, rent, kids, curiosity doors), but **professional, intelligent, interesting, restrained** writing. **No marketing copy feel** — honest about mixed/qualified results, not forced wins. Peer: `interfaces/blog-erft-recursive-fidelity-2026-09.html` (`/ship-blog/erft-recursive-fidelity`). Vitality peer still useful for access stakes. Do **not** name third-party magazines. Do **not** write mid-body “what this does not claim” sections; **Soft Story count in body = 0** (honesty rail may name the tier); park CODATA / PRA / ENGINE_SHELF in the end honesty rail only. Do **not** use empty workshops / empty rooms / quieter benches as unemployment stand-ins — say paychecks, laid off, job boards.
2. **Length:** ≥ **800** article prose words inside `<article>` after stripping nav, honesty rail, footer, and CTA row (revised from 900 to match ERFT standard). Helper: `lib/ship-blog-magazine.mjs` (`SHIP_BLOG_MIN_ARTICLE_WORDS`).
3. **Honesty rail at the end only:** one `<p class="honesty">…</p>` after the body (before or just above CTA/footer). Do not lead with honesty or sprinkle it through the piece.
4. **Structure:** kicker · headline · dateline · **problem-focused lead** · **experiment/methodology** · **hypothesis** · **results with qualifications** · **framework value** · **invitation to paper/repo** · honesty · Fair Exchange (optional short) · CTA · footer.
5. **Claims:** Keep Φ_EGS / catalog keys proportionate; full honesty stays at the end rail. **Technical sophistication without jargon overload** — explain the work clearly but respect reader intelligence.
6. **Editorial restraint:** **Professional research blog tone**, not architecture theater gimmicks. When results are mixed, say so honestly. Clear **problem → experiment → hypothesis → results → qualifications → framework value → invitation** flow.
7. **Journalism lock:** **every** `interfaces/blog-*.html` must pass `journalismVoiceSmell` (Soft Story **0**, zero refusal H2s, zero does-not-claim litigation in body, ≤2 meta jargon, no body tables, **zero empty-workshop unemployment metaphors**, **≥2 everyday-life anchors**).

CI: `tests/lib/questfest-blog.test.mjs` + `tests/lib/ship-blog-magazine.test.mjs` enforce latest-six, magazine length / honesty, and journalism voice on the full corpus.

Protocol: `protocols/QUESTFEST_SHIP_BLOG_MAGAZINE_SNAP_NSPFRNP.md`.

## When you register a paper

When you **register, protocol, or feature** a technical paper (`lib/whitepaper-registry.mjs`, `docs/*.md`):

1. **Write a magazine-grade ship-blog HTML article** under `interfaces/blog-<slug>-YYYY-MM.html` (feature prose + honesty rail **at the end** + link to the whitepaper). Voice peer: `interfaces/blog-vitality-control-rhyme-2026-09.html`.
2. **Register the note** in `lib/questfest-blog-posts.mjs` (`QUESTFEST_BLOG_POSTS[registryId]` → slug, file, headline, excerpt).
3. **Add Vercel rewrites** in `vercel.json` for `/ship-blog/<slug>` and `/ship-blog/<slug>/`.
4. **Sync the latest-six section:** `npm run sync:questfest-blog` (injects `interfaces/vibelandia-questfest.html` `#ship-blog`).
5. **Sync the interfaces index:** `npm run sync:interfaces-index`.
6. **Order is newest → oldest** (`published` date descending). Never prefer older notes over newer papers.
7. **Companions only** (one-pagers, living TOCs) may set `shipBlog: false` on the registry entry so they do not steal a latest-six slot. Main papers always get a note.

Tests fail if any of the six newest eligible papers lacks a note, if the six are not newest-first, or if any ship-blog HTML fails the magazine snap (length, honesty-at-end, or journalism voice).

Skip this only when the user explicitly says the work is not a public paper.
